# =============================================================================
# apps/ext — Environment variables
# =============================================================================
# The browser extension does NOT read any environment variables at build time
# by default. All runtime configuration (LLM provider keys, VS Code bridge
# settings, telemetry opt-in, theme) is stored in `chrome.storage.local` via
# the Settings UI and is per-user.
#
# This file is intentionally near-empty — kept so contributors know there is
# nothing to set up at the shell before running `bun run dev`.
#
# If you add build-time env vars in the future (e.g. for analytics endpoints
# baked into the bundle), document them here. WXT/Vite exposes them via
# `import.meta.env.VITE_*` — never put secrets in a browser bundle.
